{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237810-balancing-beastmen-adding-flavor-and-depth-through-natural-consequences","id":1237810,"title":"\"Balancing\" Beastmen: Adding flavor and depth through natural consequences","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-07-22T14:06:36-07:00","id":1237810,"title":"\"Balancing\" Beastmen: Adding flavor and depth through natural consequences","content":"Time and time again I see posts and arguments that paint beastmen as being just plain better that than your vanilla homo sapiens. I myself have never really seen the value of such arguments, though I will admit that it does have merit from a purely mechanical perspective. After all, if you make some wolf-man raiders by adding the Fur and Claw mutations to the Brigand QC they're going to be superior fighters, since you just made them tougher and enhanced one of their attack options. What I am suggesting is that one looks past the realm of the purely mechanical and begin to apply the natural consequences of mixing human and animal biology.<br /> <br /> Now, humans have a lot of things that set us apart in the animal kingdom aside from our intelligence. There have been a lot of videos and articles on that subject all over the internet, so I'm not going to go into them in extreme detail here. But quite a few of the common beastmen concepts have traits that can have some fairly serious impacts when looked at in respect to that. The fur/scales mutation for example, interferes with the ability to effectively regulate body heat through sweating. While many animals with fur can sweat (e.g. horses), they do so much less effectively that humans, as the fur decreases the efficiency of sweat evaporation.<br /> <br /> If one goes with the quite common route of just has their beastmen be humans with animal heads, what have you changed? In addition to the often hand-waved issue of it being unlikely that most animal's mouths would be even capable of producing human speech, there's quite a few potential problems that you've possibly introduced. Many species, particularly herbivorous ones, have eyes on the sides of their head, increasing area of vision at the cost of the losing a vanilla human's binocular vision and the amazingly precise depth perception that comes with it.<br /> <br /> So what's the point of all this? In addition to solving the &quot;problem&quot; of &quot;Why haven't beastmen out-competed baseline humans?&quot;, it gives an additional dimension to add flavor and depth to the cultures of beastmen throughout creation. I'm not advocating for strict adherence to scientific realism here, not at all. I'm not even arguing that they're should be some sort of mechanical penalties to the common mutations given to beastmen, though I personally take those consequences into account when stating beastman NPCs for my games. But adding in one or two of these little quirks to a beastman species can give players and STs a lot of room to create a unique character to NPCs and cultures. Say you have a culture of Cobramen, and you make two changes relevant to their cobra-ness; they're exothermic and obligate carnivores. How does this change their culture? Well, they're much less likely to get things done overnight and in the morning. but will be much more active in the afternoon and evening. They'll have a much smaller caloric need than a typical human, but they're going to need to get those calories from meat. That means they should have a disproportionate number of ranchers, hunters, and shepherds, with farmers (IF they have any at all) being focused solely on growing feed crops. It's also a fertile breeding ground for potential drama! What's your vegetarian immaculate monk going to do when traveling through a nation that is, by biological necessity, carnivorous? How are you going to handle things when, as a polite and hospitable gesture, you hand the wolfman ambassador a glass of wine and he dies violently convulsing while spewing fluids from both ends?<br /> <br /> Long and short, Thinking beyond the surface differences of beastmen to the logical conclusions of said differences is a good way to add flavor and drama to your games. Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":155,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","user":"Noodle","date":". 07-22-2018, 06:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-22T15:08:20-07:00","id":1237821,"title":"","content":"In a related vein, I would be thrilled to see a beastfolk tribal nation that doesn't wear clothes, because they are so heavily furred that there would be no point and clothes would actually be inconvenient. At most, they wear belts bearing bags and pouches, like Wookies.<br /> <br /> But their acute sense of smell gives them a very different set of standards for modesty and humiliation than the hairless nations. Instead of wearing clothes to preserve their modesty from the sight of others, they have a thriving perfume industry because they want to mask certain odors from each other. Such as the odors of urination and defecation, or of sexual arousal.<br /> <br /> In a parallel to facial masks, they might also use perfumes to hide fear or anger from each other, for political purposes.<br /> <br /> Anyone interacting with this people would need to take care about how they smell, as anyone appearing before them without perfume would be &quot;seen&quot; (smelled, rather) as naked. But simply wearing any perform wouldn't be quite enough either, as they developed a complicated and nuanced culture around which perfumes are appropriate for which social occasions and an individual's socioeconomic status.<br /> <br /> So rather than showing up naked to meet a king to negotiate a peace treaty, you could inadvertently show up smelling like a clown or an expectant bride or a mourning parent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-22T15:36:05-07:00","id":1237827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237810-balancing-beastmen-adding-flavor-and-depth-through-natural-consequences?p=1237821#post1237821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a related vein, I would be thrilled to see a beastfolk tribal nation that doesn't wear clothes, because they are so heavily furred that there would be no point and clothes would actually be inconvenient. At most, they wear belts bearing bags and pouches, like Wookies.<br /> <br /> But their acute sense of smell gives them a very different set of standards for modesty and humiliation than the hairless nations. Instead of wearing clothes to preserve their modesty from the sight of others, they have a thriving perfume industry because they want to mask certain odors from each other. Such as the odors of urination and defecation, or of sexual arousal.<br /> <br /> In a parallel to facial masks, they might also use perfumes to hide fear or anger from each other, for political purposes.<br /> <br /> Anyone interacting with this people would need to take care about how they smell, as anyone appearing before them without perfume would be &quot;seen&quot; (smelled, rather) as naked. But simply wearing any perform wouldn't be quite enough either, as they developed a complicated and nuanced culture around which perfumes are appropriate for which social occasions and an individual's socioeconomic status.<br /> <br /> So rather than showing up naked to meet a king to negotiate a peace treaty, you could inadvertently show up smelling like a clown or an expectant bride or a mourning parent.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am 100% stealing this for any kind of non-violent encounter with beastfolk - this is brilliant<br /> <br /> <br /> and Noodle's idea of purely carnivorous beastfolk being a challenge to vegetarian player characters - love it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T01:59:41-07:00","id":1237918,"title":"","content":"There was a brief something mentioned talking about Raksi's ape-men in the write-up for Sperimin I always use. It talks about how her Ape-Men are lacking &quot;all the beauty and grace of the hybrid, which Gaia granted to the grandchildren of her lover, Luna&quot; because Raksi hates all beautiful things, and has systematically slaughtered all but the ugliest of every generation. Until only the hideous and the misshapen are left.<br /> <br /> I always took it to mean that Gaia, in her guise as the Emerald Mother, pulled some strings to ensure that the Beastfolk born of Lunars get the best of both worlds, and by extension that any beastfolk NOT arising from Lunars (the Demesnes or Wyld-mutated) lacked this subtle benefit. Now that EX3 explicitly has Beastfolk who aren't the product of Lunars, this is what I'm doing. The snake-folk of the Southeast, as not-Lunar-Beastfolk are going to be stuck being cold-blooded and with dietary issues. Gaia doesn't love them out of love for Luna, so they're boned compared to Lunar snake-men, who are warm-blooded and possess dentition that allows for a normal omnivorous diet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","name":"Wyldwraith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T05:54:47-07:00","id":1237937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What's your vegetarian immaculate monk going to do when traveling through a nation that is, by biological necessity, carnivorous? </div> </div> </div>If he's a good Immaculate? Smoke everyone, because beastmen are Anathema. If he's a bad Immaculate, I'm pretty sure knowingly associating with Anathema is a greater heresy than eating meat.<br /> <br /> Beastmen haven't out-competed normal humans because there are a lot more humans than beastmen, and mutations usually aren't enough to make up for a primitive tech base and lack of formal training. If a human soldier and a wolf-man were equipped and trained equally, the wolf would probably win, but the whole point is that they <b>won't</b> be equipped and trained equally unless they've got Lunar backing.<br /> <br /> If they have Lunar backing, you have way bigger problems than their baseline troops being a bit better.<br /> <br /> That aside, above and beyond the physical downsides, there are psychological barriers that might keep beastmen on the back foot. A tiger-man is certainly bad news, but tigers, compared to humans, just aren't good at organizing into large groups. Maybe they're just too competitive,, surly and greedy to get things together unless they're forced to? Pack hunters might be better at coordination, but quicker to break and run when things go badly (give them better Drill than most beastman hordes if the warband is primarily the same species, but always make Morale checks as if they had -1 Drill).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24387-amayad","name":"Amayad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T07:47:29-07:00","id":1237960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amayad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237810-balancing-beastmen-adding-flavor-and-depth-through-natural-consequences?p=1237937#post1237937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If he's a good Immaculate? Smoke everyone, because beastmen are Anathema. If he's a bad Immaculate, I'm pretty sure knowingly associating with Anathema is a greater heresy than eating meat.<br /> <br /> Beastmen haven't out-competed normal humans because there are a lot more humans than beastmen, and mutations usually aren't enough to make up for a primitive tech base and lack of formal training. If a human soldier and a wolf-man were equipped and trained equally, the wolf would probably win, but the whole point is that they <b>won't</b> be equipped and trained equally unless they've got Lunar backing.<br /> <br /> If they have Lunar backing, you have way bigger problems than their baseline troops being a bit better.<br /> <br /> That aside, above and beyond the physical downsides, there are psychological barriers that might keep beastmen on the back foot. A tiger-man is certainly bad news, but tigers, compared to humans, just aren't good at organizing into large groups. Maybe they're just too competitive,, surly and greedy to get things together unless they're forced to? Pack hunters might be better at coordination, but quicker to break and run when things go badly (give them better Drill than most beastman hordes if the warband is primarily the same species, but always make Morale checks as if they had -1 Drill).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Beastmen, as of 3e, are no longer consider subjects to genocide by the realm by default--we have a god of a beastmen tribe training immaculates in Parsaad, and IIRC a beastfolk monk now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T08:01:26-07:00","id":1237964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237810-balancing-beastmen-adding-flavor-and-depth-through-natural-consequences?p=1237960#post1237960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Beastmen, as of 3e, are no longer consider subjects to genocide by the realm by default--we have a god of a beastmen tribe training immaculates in Parsaad, and IIRC a beastfolk monk now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt they ever were, and they've certainly never been Anathema.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T08:15:49-07:00","id":1237968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wyldwraith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237810-balancing-beastmen-adding-flavor-and-depth-through-natural-consequences?p=1237918#post1237918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always took it to mean that Gaia, in her guise as the Emerald Mother, pulled some strings to ensure that the Beastfolk born of Lunars get the best of both worlds, and by extension that any beastfolk NOT arising from Lunars (the Demesnes or Wyld-mutated) lacked this subtle benefit. Now that EX3 explicitly has Beastfolk who aren't the product of Lunars, this is what I'm doing. The snake-folk of the Southeast, as not-Lunar-Beastfolk are going to be stuck being cold-blooded and with dietary issues. Gaia doesn't love them out of love for Luna, so they're boned compared to Lunar snake-men, who are warm-blooded and possess dentition that allows for a normal omnivorous diet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well Lunar-created beastmen are different in 3E. They're not the offspring of Lunars. Instead, they are humans who passed a Lunar's trial/initiation and were blessed with beastmen mutations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T08:23:21-07:00","id":1237972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237810-balancing-beastmen-adding-flavor-and-depth-through-natural-consequences?p=1237964#post1237964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I doubt they ever were, and they've certainly never been Anathema.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except when they are.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Immaculates apply the technical term Anathema\u2014in the Realm it\u2019s a formal clerical finding\u2014to anything that the order finds abhorrent to stable and prosperous life. Solar and Lunar Exalted are always Anathema; the label can also potentially encompass Fair Folk, beastmen, elementals, and demons who threaten Realm interests, as well as gods and their Exigent champions in open rebellion against the Immaculate Philosophy.&quot;<br /> <br /> Page 74, corebook.<br /> <br /> Given that Beastmen are quite often threatening Realm interests (because the Realm's interests involve dominating all it surveys), I imagine quite a few Immaculates get..Twitchy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24387-amayad","name":"Amayad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T08:26:01-07:00","id":1237974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amayad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237810-balancing-beastmen-adding-flavor-and-depth-through-natural-consequences?p=1237972#post1237972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except when they are.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Immaculates apply the technical term Anathema\u2014in the Realm it\u2019s a formal clerical finding\u2014to anything that the order finds abhorrent to stable and prosperous life. Solar and Lunar Exalted are always Anathema; the label can also potentially encompass Fair Folk, beastmen, elementals, and demons who threaten Realm interests, as well as gods and their Exigent champions in open rebellion against the Immaculate Philosophy.&quot;<br /> <br /> Page 74, corebook.<br /> <br /> Given that Beastmen are quite often threatening Realm interests (because the Realm's interests involve dominating all it surveys), I imagine quite a few Immaculates get..Twitchy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Certainly their are beastmen who are anathema--the ones that lead revolutions or the like--but just as there are Exigents who are welcome to the immaculate philosphy, there are beastfolk who are as well. After Solars and Lunars, the Anathema label is case by case it seems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T08:47:18-07:00","id":1237979,"title":"","content":"They can declare <i>dragon blooded</i> anathema if they really need to. Beastmen probably have to do less to get slapped with it, but that's it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T08:57:27-07:00","id":1237980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amayad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237810-balancing-beastmen-adding-flavor-and-depth-through-natural-consequences?p=1237937#post1237937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If he's a good Immaculate? Smoke everyone, because beastmen are Anathema. If he's a bad Immaculate, I'm pretty sure knowingly associating with Anathema is a greater heresy than eating meat.<br /> <br /> Beastmen haven't out-competed normal humans because there are a lot more humans than beastmen, and mutations usually aren't enough to make up for a primitive tech base and lack of formal training. If a human soldier and a wolf-man were equipped and trained equally, the wolf would probably win, but the whole point is that they <b>won't</b> be equipped and trained equally unless they've got Lunar backing.<br /> <br /> If they have Lunar backing, you have way bigger problems than their baseline troops being a bit better.<br /> <br /> That aside, above and beyond the physical downsides, there are psychological barriers that might keep beastmen on the back foot. A tiger-man is certainly bad news, but tigers, compared to humans, just aren't good at organizing into large groups. Maybe they're just too competitive,, surly and greedy to get things together unless they're forced to? Pack hunters might be better at coordination, but quicker to break and run when things go badly (give them better Drill than most beastman hordes if the warband is primarily the same species, but always make Morale checks as if they had -1 Drill).</div> </div> </div> </div>Beast people are not Anathema. The only beings that are guaranteed Anathema are the Solar and Lunar Exalted. A beastperson would need to do some heinous stuff, very consistently, to be made Anathema. The Realm are not a bunch of lolevil monsters, the Immaculate Order is not a bunch of religious fanatics from shithammer 40k looking for a reason to genocide their inferiors. The Monks are far, FAR more likely to make a trip to convert a nation of Beastpeople than send the Hunt in to genocide them.<br /> <br /> (That the process of conversion would itself likely often be terrible because Imperialism is kinda inherently awful is a whole different matter).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T09:00:56-07:00","id":1237982,"title":"","content":"Hmm, resist the urge to play a game of duelling goalpost shifts...<br /> <br /> I'll admit that out of all of the things that Third Edition added to the expanded definition of Anathema, I had forgotten that beastfolk were included. In my defence, they have to be at the bottom of that list of ghosts and spirits and Exalted, if not outright out of place in it. And my comment was in reference to prior Editions, but I was still somewhat incorrect.<br /> <br /> I would still maintain that I was less incorrect than the assertion that beastfolk qualify as Anathema by default, to the point that assertions of a general genocidal policy is in effect (especially considering the parrotman Immaculate monk that is actually living on the Blessed isle), and that to apply the label to absolutely anybody that opposes the Realm feels a bit spurious.<br /> <br /> Although honestly, I've still got to find that just about anything beastfolk would do places them on that list. It makes sense that the Philosophy would see cosmological and spiritual implications from even general political opposition from those other entities, but beastfolk are just line backers with skin conditions. Seeing a threat in them to the divinely ordained supremacy of the Dragon Blooded doesn't quite make sense to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237810-balancing-beastmen-adding-flavor-and-depth-through-natural-consequences?p=1237979#post1237979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They can declare <i>dragon blooded</i> anathema if they really need to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to vehemently disagree with this, but I also want to review the case of those red jade short daiklaves wielded by the murderous rogue monk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T11:03:20-07:00","id":1238013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237810-balancing-beastmen-adding-flavor-and-depth-through-natural-consequences?p=1237980#post1237980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Realm are not a bunch of lolevil monsters, the Immaculate Order is not a bunch of religious fanatics from shithammer 40k looking for a reason to genocide their inferiors. The Monks are far, FAR more likely to make a trip to convert a nation of Beastpeople than send the Hunt in to genocide them.</div> </div> </div> </div>This statement is unfortunately countered by individuals like Peleps Deled. While he is definitely not the norm, it's highly unlikely he is the sole fanatic in the order. The problem is compounded because Deled holds a position of some authority. So while I agree that the IO is not a bunch of religious fanatics as a whole, they do have a presence in the Order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T11:25:58-07:00","id":1238019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237810-balancing-beastmen-adding-flavor-and-depth-through-natural-consequences?p=1238013#post1238013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This statement is unfortunately countered by individuals like Peleps Deled. While he is definitely not the norm, it's highly unlikely he is the sole fanatic in the order. The problem is compounded because Deled holds a position of some authority. So while I agree that the IO is not a bunch of religious fanatics as a whole, they do have a presence in the Order.</div> </div> </div> </div>Peleps Deled counters nothing. My statement is that portraying the Order as predominantly fanatics is stupid shit that fits better in 40k. All Faiths, with <i>no exceptions,</i> have fanatical members willing to kill. <i>Atheism</i> has insane fanatics. Peleps Deled is meaningless in regards to my point that the Immaculate Order is not a faith of fanatics, but rather of true believers doing the best according to their faith and conscience.<br /> <br /> That this <i>still</i> makes them a power of imperialism and danger in the world is a tragic truth that power structures and imperialism are often dangerous, monstrous things, regardless of the good intent of the average person who makes it up, systems subverting people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T14:47:02-07:00","id":1238065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237810-balancing-beastmen-adding-flavor-and-depth-through-natural-consequences?p=1238013#post1238013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is compounded because Deled holds a position of some authority.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I'm not sure of the entirety of how various fictions and comics have developed Deled's position, but the story that introduced him was fairly clear on the idea that he was being promoted into an assignment to Antarctica.<br /> <br /> Mind... I need to look at the Aspect Book stuff again to see how it compares, because another detail of significance there was how his fanaticism was pointed inwards at the Order itself, and it made his fellow monks hold him in contempt.<br /> <br /> Really, he's something of a weird example of religious fanaticism considering how much the narrative has portrayed his violent extremes as something that the institutions disavow, rather than being enabled and empowered by them.<br /> <br /> The Immaculate Order not being without its issues, especially with how the current Edition seems to be going for a feel of Grammaton Clerics blended with Dai Li, but Peleps Deled is not the most apparent or sophisticated of them (even if he's broad enough to easily become an Internet legend).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T15:22:50-07:00","id":1238073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237810-balancing-beastmen-adding-flavor-and-depth-through-natural-consequences?p=1238019#post1238019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Peleps Deled counters nothing. My statement is that portraying the Order as predominantly fanatics is stupid shit that fits better in 40k. All Faiths, with <i>no exceptions,</i> have fanatical members willing to kill. <i>Atheism</i> has insane fanatics. Peleps Deled is meaningless in regards to my point that the Immaculate Order is not a faith of fanatics, but rather of true believers doing the best according to their faith and conscience.<br /> <br /> That this <i>still</i> makes them a power of imperialism and danger in the world is a tragic truth that power structures and imperialism are often dangerous, monstrous things, regardless of the good intent of the average person who makes it up, systems subverting people.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're missing the point. The Order does have a faction of zealots/fanatics, and It's not limited to Deled. In the novel where Swan and Arianna met, a Dragonblood killed a man and set fire to an inn. All because the man asked why he was interested in a library on the edge of town. It was outright murder, and several more died in the fire the Dragonblood set. Reading back into some of that Dragonbloods dialogue, he was clearly a fanatic (and a homicidal one at that). As I said, the IO is not just a group of fanatics. For the most part, the majority of the IO are good, if ignorant, people who want to help make Creation a better place. However, Deled and this one Dragonblood in the novel are not isolated incidents. There are several Wyld Hunts present across many novels and other tidbits of lore, that acted in a similar manner. The Wyld Hunt is an arm of the Immaculate Order, and the Hunt seems to have an inordinate amount of homicidal/genocidal nut-jobs!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T15:48:56-07:00","id":1238080,"title":"","content":"Was that novel any good?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T15:51:20-07:00","id":1238082,"title":"","content":"Rather, the Wyld Hunt would be the natural dumping ground for the Immaculate Order\u2019s rare sociopaths, leading to a statistically non-representative higher ratio of madmen in the Order\u2019s militant branch of people most likely to die and stop being a problem for anyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T22:26:30-07:00","id":1238136,"title":"","content":"I don't know if I can square this new supposedly friendlier Immaculate Order with the realities of Creation:<br /> 1) Many, many Immaculates are not in fact Dragon Blooded. Further, even in areas the Realm has nominal control of, there are many places the Immaculate Order is considered bad, if for no other reason than their &quot;Beat divine ass to make gods get with the Immaculate program, and stop mugging for more worshippers by interfering in Creation&quot; reputation is going to make any population particularly devout rather defensive. Harborhead is a great example of this. The Realm may have control, and the Leopard Throne has a Realm puppet on it, but the Ten Tribes are Ahlat-worshippers, and that's IT. Trying to convert them ends badly, to the point the Realm uses religious provocation to deliberately cause riots they can then violently suppress. My point here isn't this 2E text-read of the Realm's religious provocation-tactic...It's that, in a place with people as devout as the people of Harborhead, it's a lot easier for a small misstep to blossom into violence. A mortal monk doesn't have a Terrestrial Exaltation to fall back on, so I'd expect his set-point for violence to be lower out of increased self-consciousness of vulnerability.<br /> <br /> 2) Continuing with these mortal Immaculates, the supernatural is lots more dangerous to them than it is their Dragon Blooded counterparts. I would ALWAYS expect a mortal Immaculate to be &quot;quicker to pull the trigger&quot; when a hint of supernatural threat presents itself, because they know if THEY get hit first, they're probably finished. Increased potential for violence through awareness of squishiness. That elemental may just be angrily mouthing off, resentful of its place in Immaculate-dominated territory, but the monks can't read its mind. They see its angry, they see its yelling, and they know that earth elemental is VERY strong. Where a Dragon Blooded monk might say &quot;Let's wait a minute longer, and see if we can't defuse the situation without the need to eliminate a valuable contributor to this area&quot; the mortals don't have the kind of power that will let them walk off that elemental's punch even if it lands. They're going to be more likely to deem the elemental an imminent threat sooner rather than later, and respond accordingly. This gives them a reputation with the locals as being too quick to pull the trigger.<br /> <br /> 3) Dragon Blooded and mortal Immaculates alike, they believe, deeply, that they are RIGHT. The Immaculate Philosophy isn't optional. You are either a follower of the One True Path to Enlightenment, or you are, at best, in need of conversion. If you respond (in their opinion) negatively to the subsequent conversion attempt, you are WILLFULLY turning from the One True Path into apostasy. I don't consider them all nutjobs. I consider them like medieval Catholics with extensive kung-fu training. While non-adherence might be more tolerated in the illiterate foreign peasants (for a time), the SAME level of non-adherence from someone whose visibly &quot;middle class&quot; or better, educated, or politically significant will NOT be tolerated. It can't be, because those are the kind of people the local peasantry look to, and take their cues from. If an Immaculate doesn't come down hard on the guy who owns the small town's one major store for saying he thinks the IP is bullshit, and by come down hard, I mean break bones(at best), they risk next week having six customers with a bit of time to shoot the shit while making their purchases starting to say the same thing. This isn't blind fanaticism, it's monotheism with zero tolerance for diverging belief systems. This is worsened by the fact that the culture of the Realm explicitly adopts a White Man's Burden sort of approach to less affluent, less frankly Blessed Isle locations controlled by the Realm. While I accept that EX3's doing stuff like Immaculates no longer tolerating counter-productive practices like Dragon Blooded rape-tourism in An-Teng is realistic, I can't see believable Immaculates ever considering local law and custom meaningful barriers to Dragon Blooded. Satrapies are places where the local powers agreed to be Satrapies because the Realm can beat their ass. The number of places in the Threshold that actually want the Realm there is small, so the local resentment is always going to bias the Immaculates towards &quot;their&quot; people. If a Dragon Blooded says &quot;I heard these four men conspiring to ambush and rob me, so I struck them down&quot; the Immaculate is going to believe the Dragon Blooded over the eleven local witnesses to the slayings. The Immaculate &quot;knows&quot; the locals are &quot;against THEM&quot; so the Dragon Blooded's story seems more plausible to the Immaculate...and this is if the Immaculate actually adheres to the tenets of his faith and isn't corrupt.<br /> <br /> 4) The Realm is a police-state. The name &quot;The All-Seeing Eye&quot; pretty much screams &quot;secret police of the state&quot; from the mountaintops. Except, there's no division of Church and State in the Realm. It's explicitly designed that way, because Chejop Kejak wields the Church to influence the Empress-controlled State. With the Empress gone, and Chejop Kejak still here puppeting the Mouth of Peace, it is inevitable that Church scope has begun to creep over the borders into the State. The Empress designed that State to rely on her, so the State is crippled to an extent without her. More creep by Church into State. Immaculates are going to be informed in their behavior by the fact the Church is growing stronger in SOME ways, even as the State falters due to divisions among the Houses. The same Houses that are de-funding the Wyld Hunt, and pulling its members for the well-understood motive of using those members in the struggle for the throne. The Immaculates are going to perceive this as a time when the Realm's faith is faltering out of the Dynasts succumbing en masse to the temporal temptation to pursue secular power over spiritual purity. That's bound to make individuals who have devoted their lives to this religion feel more desperate, and desperate people are very, very often violent people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","name":"Wyldwraith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T22:49:10-07:00","id":1238140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237810-balancing-beastmen-adding-flavor-and-depth-through-natural-consequences?p=1238080#post1238080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was that novel any good?</div> </div> </div> </div>It was... not bad. It's actually the novel where the Bull of the North defeats the Tepet Legions. Magma Kraken is used to an impressive effect against a large unit of Realm infantry. Swan's a pretty decent character. I didn't really care for Arianna though. Her cold dismissive nature for Swan, who saved her life, is a bit off-putting. Especially considering she begins pining for him the moment he leaves her!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T23:16:00-07:00","id":1238145,"title":"","content":"Something I'd like to posit which I've seen touched upon but not addressed, is the fact that while beastmen may not be directly outlawed by the Immaculate Faith, one has to wonder about the cultural implications. Imagine if you will, if one of the ever-present dangers of your nation are ravening foreigners with the guile of humans and the brutal savagery of beasts. I don't know about you, but that is fertile ground for prejudice, especially if tied into a neat bow with zealous preachers and tales of Immaculate heroes facing off against the Anathema, many of which surround themselves with such vassals and soldiers. At least that's the way I see the issue.<br /> <br /> Another prospect I noticed that hasn't raised is the potential of beastmen derived from folktales and anecdotes from antiquity and myth. Many such creatures exist, and many are shown to be brutal, stupid, but dangerous people, with strange customs and wondrous wealth. So much untapped possibility, and so often, it's merely window dressing to further show off how bizarre their patron Lunar or god is. This is coming from apparently one of the few fans of the Thousand Stream River of 2e, but they can be so much more. <br /> <br /> Finally, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar155_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"155\" data-vbnamecard=\"155\">Noodle</a>, I noticed you didn't bring up the various attempts in your games of Wardens of Gaia and various Twilights attempting to produce &quot;better&quot; humans, and the various wrinkles you threw their way. Needless to say, I found the hulking musclebound brutes that arose from their attempts to be at least relevant to the discussion.<br /> <br /> That's at least my two cents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T02:03:59-07:00","id":1238157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wyldwraith</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">supposedly friendlier Immaculate Order</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> Where on Earth are you getting that?<br /> <br /> I get if you don't recognise references if I compare them to the Grammaton Clerics and the freakin' Dai Li, but from where are you getting the idea that anybody has referred to them as friendlier?<br /> <br /> Mind, it begs the question of &quot;friendlier than what&quot;; the Immaculate Order that has ever existed in the books, or the one that happens to exist in the imagination of any given reader. </span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T08:37:54-07:00","id":1238238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237810-balancing-beastmen-adding-flavor-and-depth-through-natural-consequences?p=1238073#post1238073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're missing the point. The Order does have a faction of zealots/fanatics, and It's not limited to Deled. In the novel where Swan and Arianna met, a Dragonblood killed a man and set fire to an inn. All because the man asked why he was interested in a library on the edge of town. It was outright murder, and several more died in the fire the Dragonblood set. Reading back into some of that Dragonbloods dialogue, he was clearly a fanatic (and a homicidal one at that). As I said, the IO is not just a group of fanatics. For the most part, the majority of the IO are good, if ignorant, people who want to help make Creation a better place. However, Deled and this one Dragonblood in the novel are not isolated incidents. There are several Wyld Hunts present across many novels and other tidbits of lore, that acted in a similar manner. The Wyld Hunt is an arm of the Immaculate Order, and the Hunt seems to have an inordinate amount of homicidal/genocidal nut-jobs!</div> </div> </div> </div>I would not accept such a novel as a remotely accurate representation of the Order. It sounds like some freelancer skimming Exalted and seeing &quot;Oh, the evil religious faction&quot; and spewing shit onto the page.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T10:05:42-07:00","id":1238263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237810-balancing-beastmen-adding-flavor-and-depth-through-natural-consequences?p=1238238#post1238238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would not accept such a novel as a remotely accurate representation of the Order. It sounds like some freelancer skimming Exalted and seeing &amp;quot;Oh, the evil religious faction&amp;quot; and spewing shit onto the page.</div> </div> </div> </div>Several novels portray the Hunts in a very similar fashion. Those novels were also considered canon material, to the point that later sourcebooks referenced events that happened in those same novels! Of those novels, 1 series was a 1E product, the other 2 were during 2E. So it's been a consistent representation so far.<br /> <br /> I don't believe the Order overall is full of homocidal/genocidal wack-a-doodles. Most of the crazies seem to be consolidated in the Wyld Hunt branch as well. Perhaps that is a conscious move by the order to put the psychos where they'll do the most good, and least harm to the Order's image.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T10:36:42-07:00","id":1238274,"title":"","content":"Also, if you're a fanatic who loves killing people... what part of the Immaculate Order are you going to try to get put in? Helping the poor? Being a preacher who wanders between peasant villages? Missionary?* Assistant to a senior monk in a temple in a Realm city? Or being a holy warrior who hunts down and slays demons? <br /> Whereas someone who wants to be a monk because they really care about helping people advance in the cycle of reincarnation is probably not going to be so interested. Someone who wants to help the poor may not be someone who wants to &quot;do whatever it takes&quot; to find and slay anathema.<br /> <br /> <br /> *Okay, you may well want to be a missionary. The senior Immaculates may decide that more liberal sorts who are happy to break out some syncretism are more effective. So they may prefer to put you in the section where your fanaticism will ensure you won't be seduced by an Anathema's pleas for mercy. Though it depends; I'm sure there's fanatical missionaries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T11:03:55-07:00","id":1238283,"title":"","content":"I did say such a thing in post 19.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T11:06:05-07:00","id":1238284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237810-balancing-beastmen-adding-flavor-and-depth-through-natural-consequences?p=1238263#post1238263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Several novels portray the Hunts in a very similar fashion. Those novels were also considered canon material, to the point that later sourcebooks referenced events that happened in those same novels! Of those novels, 1 series was a 1E product, the other 2 were during 2E. So it's been a consistent representation so far.<br /> <br /> I don't believe the Order overall is full of homocidal/genocidal wack-a-doodles. Most of the crazies seem to be consolidated in the Wyld Hunt branch as well. Perhaps that is a conscious move by the order to put the psychos where they'll do the most good, and least harm to the Order's image.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good reason not to read the Exalted novels. You know what else used to be canon? Pedo Dynasts raped by their mothers who now rape children with thorny vines. Underworld rape camps where the ghosts of rapists are raped for all eternity. Third Circle Demons gangraping new Infernals. Ma-Ha-Suchi creating rape camps and enslaving women to be raped by wolves.<br /> <br /> &quot;It was canon&quot; isn't a valid argument for a shitty setting piece. The people who wrote the novels and tons of the sourcebooks were utter hacks relying on shock value and grimdark EEEEVIL Dragonblooded as the twisted charachitures for the glorious Solar PCs to fight. Fuck the novels, fuck the old Sourcebooks. They're shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T11:33:28-07:00","id":1238300,"title":"","content":"I find it amusing that an off-hand line about an immaculate traveling through a beastman nation towards the end of my post has ballooned like this.<br /> <br /> My personal opinion is that, given the Immaculate Order\u2019s belief in reincarnation being affected by a karma-like enlightenment, being born as a beastman is seen by the religion as being a punishment from the dragons for misdeeds from your previous life. Something along the lines of them saying \u201cYou behaved as a beast before, so now you shall take its visage for all to see.\u201d Some immaculates may even go so far as to suggest that the particular type of beastman you are is representative of your past life\u2019s sins. As such, I get the feeling that most immaculates would say that beastmen must then work harder and more diligently in service to the dragons and the dragon bloods to atone for their \u2018misdeeds\u2019. If they do that, great! If they fall into sin again, cavorting with demons, worshiping false idols, or serving anathema, well, then you may have to put them down, lest they fall further from the dragon\u2019s grace. For their own spiritual good. <br /> <br /> Of course, the Order is made up up people, and some Monks may attempt to \u2018correct\u2019 some heretical behavior while others may use that same behavior as an excuse to put them down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T14:18:54-07:00","id":1238367,"title":"","content":"Anyway, original topic:<br /> <br /> Towards the end of Second Edition, I had a greater liking for the idea that beastfolk had a balancing act of positive and negative mutations in the same manner as the Polar mutants of Autochthonia. Partially because I thought it was a more interesting way to design mutants, partially to alleviate a sense that they were strictly superior.<br /> <br /> These days, well, I'll reserve full judgement until I see what the list of Merits that mutations consist of, and whatever other benefits that might be bestowed on beastfolk by Lunars or other sources, but my general impulse is that it's not strictly necessary. It can be interesting in some cases to say that people with the traits of, say, tigers are limited to the consumption of meat, but on the whole I think it's a very drastic step, and the kind of thing that might overwhelm the portrayal of individuals and groups as a whole.<br /> <br /> The argument of being out-competed... I'm unconcerned with. The interactions of various human societies is sufficiently complex to not make it a big deal. Especially if a lot of beastfolk amount to people who are distinct looking but only have mundane physical Merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T14:25:57-07:00","id":1238369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237810-balancing-beastmen-adding-flavor-and-depth-through-natural-consequences?p=1238367#post1238367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, original topic:<br /> <br /> Towards the end of Second Edition, I had a greater liking for the idea that beastfolk had a balancing act of positive and negative mutations in the same manner as the Polar mutants of Autochthonia. Partially because I thought it was a more interesting way to design mutants, partially to alleviate a sense that they were strictly superior.<br /> <br /> These days, well, I'll reserve full judgement until I see what the list of Merits that mutations consist of, and whatever other benefits that might be bestowed on beastfolk by Lunars or other sources, but my general impulse is that it's not strictly necessary. It can be interesting in some cases to say that people with the traits of, say, tigers are limited to the consumption of meat, but on the whole I think it's a very drastic step, and the kind of thing that might overwhelm the portrayal of individuals and groups as a whole.<br /> <br /> The argument of being out-competed... I'm unconcerned with. The interactions of various human societies is sufficiently complex to not make it a big deal. Especially if a lot of beastfolk amount to people who are distinct looking but only have mundane physical Merits.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it helps, we can make beastfolk pretty great out of the book. Unusual hide 2, Natural Weapons 4, Fleet of Foot 4 makes a pretty good Raksi ape person, for example, someone really fast, with deadly nature weapons, and a little extra soak from their thick fur and hide. Of course, these are all glaringly obvious, so you're gonna probably face some nasty discrimination out of Raksi's territory. And within, well, you did her creepy witch trials to become a badass super soldier! Enjoy!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T14:51:54-07:00","id":1238378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237810-balancing-beastmen-adding-flavor-and-depth-through-natural-consequences?p=1238369#post1238369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it helps, we can make beastfolk pretty great out of the book. Unusual hide 2, Natural Weapons 4, Fleet of Foot 4 makes a pretty good Raksi ape person, for example, someone really fast, with deadly nature weapons, and a little extra soak from their thick fur and hide.</div> </div> </div> </div>That raises an interesting question: the character creation rules afford access to the full range of Merits, including supernatural ones that can be collectively utilised to represent one's character as a certain kind of beastperson or similar mutant, sooo\u2026 does it make sense to assume that the character comes from a society in which everybody has such endowments? Or might they be considered to be somebody that has the luck of their particular phenotype's draw?<br /> <br /> It also raises the more mundane question of: wasn't the higher version of Natural Weapons something that let you shoot quills and the like? I legitimately cannot remember, and can't check at the moment.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T15:02:57-07:00","id":1238380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237810-balancing-beastmen-adding-flavor-and-depth-through-natural-consequences?p=1238378#post1238378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That raises an interesting question: the character creation rules afford access to the full range of Merits, including supernatural ones that can be collectively utilised to represent one's character as a certain kind of beastperson or similar mutant, sooo\u2026 does it make sense to assume that the character comes from a society in which everybody has such endowments? Or might they be considered to be somebody that has the luck of their particular phenotype's draw?<br /> <br /> It also raises the more mundane question of: wasn't the higher version of Natural Weapons something that let you shoot quills and the like? I legitimately cannot remember, and can't check at the moment.</div> </div> </div> </div>It turns your natural weapons into Medium weapons instead of light, and lets you do lethal unarmed. And I'd say that the character only comes from such a society if the player wants. Otherwise, wyld mutation or a Lunar mom or a Sorcerous accident or any other myriad ways you might have 3 dots unusual hide, 3-dot wings, and 4-dot eagle talons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T15:22:12-07:00","id":1238390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237810-balancing-beastmen-adding-flavor-and-depth-through-natural-consequences?p=1238380#post1238380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It turns your natural weapons into Medium weapons instead of light, and lets you do lethal unarmed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah yes, that's the ticket.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I'd say that the character only comes from such a society if the player wants. Otherwise, wyld mutation or a Lunar mom or a Sorcerous accident or any other myriad ways you might have 3 dots unusual hide, 3-dot wings, and 4-dot eagle talons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nono, I get that. What I'm saying is, if one does want to make a character whose background is coming from a society of mutants, and models that with an arrangement of fairly powerful Merits, does it make sense to assume that those Merits are the norm in their society?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T17:51:05-07:00","id":1238429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237810-balancing-beastmen-adding-flavor-and-depth-through-natural-consequences?p=1238390#post1238390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah yes, that's the ticket.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Nono, I get that. What I'm saying is, if one does want to make a character whose background is coming from a society of mutants, and models that with an arrangement of fairly powerful Merits, does it make sense to assume that those Merits are the norm in their society?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that'd be kinda setting warping, I think, unless it's some isolated tribe. Like, there shouldn't be 50,000 beastmen with 10 dots of fighty merits sitting around. 500 would be fine, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T18:12:06-07:00","id":1238438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237810-balancing-beastmen-adding-flavor-and-depth-through-natural-consequences?p=1238429#post1238429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, that'd be kinda setting warping, I think, unless it's some isolated tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Excellent, I believe that we're in agreement.<br /> <br /> I imagine that the difference between a wolf-person with functional and dangerous claws and elongated but ultimately superficial fingernails is much like variations that create different aptitudes for athletic skill.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T18:25:17-07:00","id":1238453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237810-balancing-beastmen-adding-flavor-and-depth-through-natural-consequences?p=1238438#post1238438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Excellent, I believe that we're in agreement.<br /> <br /> I imagine that the difference between a wolf-person with functional and dangerous claws and elongated but ultimately superficial fingernails is much like variations that create different aptitudes for athletic skill.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much, yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T04:34:27-07:00","id":1238553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237810-balancing-beastmen-adding-flavor-and-depth-through-natural-consequences?p=1238429#post1238429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, that'd be kinda setting warping, I think, unless it's some isolated tribe. Like, there shouldn't be 50,000 beastmen with 10 dots of fighty merits sitting around. 500 would be fine, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, your PC could also luck out of bad mutations rather than lucking into good ones. Maybe there are a bunch of stag-beetle boys out there with Thick Hide 5 and Natural Weapons 4, but they have some combination of restrictive diet and poor temperature tolerances that keep them burrowed into primeval trees in the Far Northeast. PC-material examples are the lucky few that can visit conventionally habitable biomes without fainting in about ten minutes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24387-amayad","name":"Amayad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T15:37:08-07:00","id":1239459,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a> <br /> Apologies, my post wasn't really meant to connect to yours. It was a general observation about the IO, after reading a bunch of stuff in the pre-Core Q&amp;A's, where the IO came up a bunch. I saw repeated over and over the focus on how the Immaculates are supposedly more flexible, understanding and tolerant. Decrying Dragon-Blooded rape-tourism in An-Teng, poo pooing Dragon Blooded that want to go mess with the Beastfolk civilization, and I started thinking about reasons why even well-intentioned Immaculates would often prove violent and intolerant while in the Threshold. I had absolute no issue with your characterization of them, and I should've been more clear about that. My sincerest apologies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","name":"Wyldwraith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T04:34:25-07:00","id":1240796,"title":"","content":"I do love some beastman/demihuman additions to my game settings! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Would you say that your beastmen could also be Exalted?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T09:11:47-07:00","id":1240905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237810-balancing-beastmen-adding-flavor-and-depth-through-natural-consequences?p=1240796#post1240796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would you say that your beastmen could also be Exalted?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why couldn't they be?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T10:03:25-07:00","id":1240924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237810-balancing-beastmen-adding-flavor-and-depth-through-natural-consequences?p=1240905#post1240905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why couldn't they be?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd think that they most definitely could be, and of any type. <br /> <br /> But, I'm pretty pro-beastly when it comes to such things. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I brought it up, because if we're having a game-and-setting balance discussion, beastmen being unable to be Chosen is a pretty major disadvantage. Even if your average individual is tough, being unable to access Exalted (or equivalent) champions in Creation is a probable death sentence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T11:14:20-07:00","id":1240963,"title":"","content":"There's no particular reason to think they can't. They're human, they can exalt. And there a number of beastmen exalts mentioned in both 2nd and 3rd ed.<br /> <br /> Plus, if players in your Solar game want to play a beastmen, that seems pretty fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T12:37:46-07:00","id":1240991,"title":"","content":"I would think they'd have no better chance of exalting as a dragon blood than anyone in the further reaches of creation but no worse chance of exalting as anything else. <br /> <br /> Some types are off the table by their very nature (alchemical or liminal for example) bit otherwise go to town. <br /> <br /> There's probably at least one beastfolk sidereal and he'd fit right in with the gods in yu shan","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T12:52:08-07:00","id":1240997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237810-balancing-beastmen-adding-flavor-and-depth-through-natural-consequences?p=1240991#post1240991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would think they'd have no better chance of exalting as a dragon blood than anyone in the further reaches of creation but no worse chance of exalting as anything else.<br /> <br /> Some types are off the table by their very nature (alchemical or liminal for example) bit otherwise go to town.<br /> <br /> There's probably at least one beastfolk sidereal and he'd fit right in with the gods in yu shan</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Is Liminal off the table, given that Liminals are exalted when someone tries to frankenstien?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T12:56:05-07:00","id":1241000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237810-balancing-beastmen-adding-flavor-and-depth-through-natural-consequences?p=1240991#post1240991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would think they'd have no better chance of exalting as a dragon blood than anyone in the further reaches of creation but no worse chance of exalting as anything else.<br /> <br /> Some types are off the table by their very nature (alchemical or liminal for example) bit otherwise go to town.<br /> <br /> There's probably at least one beastfolk sidereal and he'd fit right in with the gods in yu shan</div> </div> </div> </div>I had two beastfolk Sidereals in my game, an orang-utan woman and a sharkman. They were buddies, because they were both a little outcast by other Sidereals (though not massively).<br /> Also, they were kids of the PCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T15:21:39-07:00","id":1241038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237810-balancing-beastmen-adding-flavor-and-depth-through-natural-consequences?p=1240997#post1240997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Is Liminal off the table, given that Liminals are exalted when someone tries to frankenstien?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that Liminals, like alchemicals, are a crafted being. Nothing says that you can't use beastman <i>parts</i> but the end result wouldn't be able to be classified as a beastman, to my mind.<br /> <br /> Also, from my understanding each liminal is linked to it's creator in some sort of permanent bond thingy. Nothing says that the creator can't be a beastman either","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T16:13:37-07:00","id":1241060,"title":"","content":"I remember that the prior developers, when they were towards the end of Second Edition, put forward an idea that beastfolk and similar mutant were less likely to Exalt, at least as Celestials, because the Essences had been programmed with a pre-disposition to avoid such people as possible Primordials sympathisers.<br /> <br /> \u2026 Maybe. I can't clearly recall the reason, just the idea that there were lower odds for mutants.<br /> <br /> Either way, I can only imagine that they also would have abandoned that idea in developing Third Edition, and any such statistics come more from the uncommonness of such people (and of them having Terrestrial ancestry consistently), rather than any prejudice on the part of the gods. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237810-balancing-beastmen-adding-flavor-and-depth-through-natural-consequences?p=1241038#post1241038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing says that you can't use beastman <i>parts</i> but the end result wouldn't be able to be classified as a beastman, to my mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>That raises the question: if a Liminal is partially composed of beastfolk parts, then does it show up in their false appearance?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T16:25:18-07:00","id":1241063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237810-balancing-beastmen-adding-flavor-and-depth-through-natural-consequences?p=1241060#post1241060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember that the prior developers, when they were towards the end of Second Edition, put forward an idea that beastfolk and similar mutant were less likely to Exalt, at least as Celestials, because the Essences had been programmed with a pre-disposition to avoid such people as possible Primordials sympathisers.<br /> <br /> \u2026 Maybe. I can't clearly recall the reason, just the idea that there were lower odds for mutants.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tbh, I don't remember that, and it doesn't really make sense. Avoiding ghost-bloods and demon-bloods would make sense, but there's no particular connection between beastmen and Primordials.<br /> <br /> I do remember though that in Scroll of Heroes, they said that Golden Children, Moon-Blessed, etc, were less likely to exalt as other kinds of Exalts.<br /> So, beastmen born (and, for a generation or two, perhaps descended) from a Lunar would be less likely to exalt as a Solar, Sidereal or Dragonblood, but more likely than average to exalt as a Lunar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 08-01-2018, 04:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T16:30:31-07:00","id":1241065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237810-balancing-beastmen-adding-flavor-and-depth-through-natural-consequences?p=1241063#post1241063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tbh, I don't remember that, and it doesn't really make sense. Avoiding ghost-bloods and demon-bloods, but there's no particular connection between<br /> <br /> I do remember though that in Scroll of Heroes, they said that Golden Children, Moon-Blessed, etc, were less likely to exalt as other kinds of Exalts.<br /> So, beastmen born (and, for a generation or two, perhaps descended) from a Lunar would be less likely to exalt as a Solar, Sidereal or Dragonblood, but more likely than average to exalt as a Lunar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beastfolk, however, are not going to be Lunar offspring in the future, or count as god-blooded even if a Lunar changes them into one. It's a rather moot point now, as far as they're concerned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T17:05:10-07:00","id":1241078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237810-balancing-beastmen-adding-flavor-and-depth-through-natural-consequences?p=1241060#post1241060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That raises the question: if a Liminal is partially composed of beastfolk parts, then does it show up in their false appearance?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was also wondering that, yeah.<br /> <br /> I suspect not. If those sorts of differences <i>did</i> show up then you'd have to curate your body parts pretty heavily to make sure your hands didn't have different skin tones from one another/other parts of your body. Let alone having a fox-face or eagle eyes or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T01:46:18-07:00","id":1241202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237810-balancing-beastmen-adding-flavor-and-depth-through-natural-consequences?p=1241065#post1241065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Beastfolk, however, are not going to be Lunar offspring in the future, or count as god-blooded even if a Lunar changes them into one. It's a rather moot point now, as far as they're concerned.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well some of them are.<br /> <br /> But either way, if we're talking about 3rd ed, I can't see the devs making a rule that beast-men are less likely to Exalt (other than due to their lower number).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T02:21:30-07:00","id":1241215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237810-balancing-beastmen-adding-flavor-and-depth-through-natural-consequences?p=1241063#post1241063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tbh, I don't remember that, and it doesn't really make sense. Avoiding ghost-bloods and demon-bloods would make sense, but there's no particular connection between beastmen and Primordials.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it was meant to be just a blanket prejudice against such modified humans, on an assumption that something weird was going on with them.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, since it was on the forum just before this one, I'm curious if you were around back then. Not for anything in particular, I just sometimes find it interesting to consider when I start to remember people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237810-balancing-beastmen-adding-flavor-and-depth-through-natural-consequences?p=1241078#post1241078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was also wondering that, yeah.<br /> <br /> I suspect not. If those sorts of differences <i>did</i> show up then you'd have to curate your body parts pretty heavily to make sure your hands didn't have different skin tones from one another/other parts of your body. Let alone having a fox-face or eagle eyes or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, I would just wonder if a dramatic addition might inform your overall ethnic appearance.<br /> <br /> I suppose for the sake of consistency, the veneer of a Liminal would be something consistent and somewhat distinct (even if probably informed by the qualities of the person or people from which they were originally made, and whose memories they'll be carrying), even if their true form is not only corpsified and gross, but they've long since switched out all of the parts.<br /> <br /> Still, there are probably Flesh Charms or something to let one alter the appearance of their veneer for some length of time, based on parts that they've taken in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T04:36:44-07:00","id":1241245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237810-balancing-beastmen-adding-flavor-and-depth-through-natural-consequences?p=1241215#post1241215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it was meant to be just a blanket prejudice against such modified humans, on an assumption that something weird was going on with them.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, since it was on the forum just before this one, I'm curious if you were around back then. Not for anything in particular, I just sometimes find it interesting to consider when I start to remember people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. I had a phoenix avatar.<br /> I posted a lot (I was one of the top 10 posters) but then stopped for a year or three*, and when I came back there was a new forum.<br /> <br /> *I don't remember why. Presumably it was after I stopped running Exalted 2nd edition, and before 3rd edition came out. I think maybe I started posting again about six months or a year before the new edition came out? When there was teasers and so on. I don't remember exactly.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T11:24:32-07:00","id":1241402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237810-balancing-beastmen-adding-flavor-and-depth-through-natural-consequences?p=1240924#post1240924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I brought it up, because if we're having a game-and-setting balance discussion, beastmen being unable to be Chosen is a pretty major disadvantage. Even if your average individual is tough, being unable to access Exalted (or equivalent) champions in Creation is a probable death sentence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they can be, but I'm not sure if it'd be a death sentence if they couldn't.<br /> <br /> Large swathes of Creation get by without Exalted champions. Creation is a big place, and with bronze age travel technology, 500 miles away might as well be on the moon for most people. There are likely places in the far Threshold that haven't seen a Dragonblood in generations, and the overwhelming majority of the world has never seen a Celestial of any stripe. Which is fine because most threats to mortals are perfectly stabbable with mundane weapons.<br /> <br /> What does a tribe near the edge of the world do when a Raksha Cataphract comes knocking? They get their spears, form up, and call for the Dog of the Unbroken Earth they've been sweet on for generations, or have their shaman call up an unbound Blood Ape to negotiate with. It's not a sure thing, it'd sure suck less if they had a Solar,, but it won't be a total curbstomp.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24387-amayad","name":"Amayad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-07T21:55:01-07:00","id":1243706,"title":"","content":"It'd be a bit of a death sentence for the purposes of playability, though, given the game is <b>Exalted</b>, not <b>Mortals</b>, and I've seen few if any mortals games that didn't culminate in exaltations being handed out and now we're playing Exalts with the background of like 20 sessions of mortal games.<br /> <br /> It'd be like playing one of those races in AD&amp;D that can't go past level 6; great fun if the game never goes past 6, but once the game is in the 10s range, you're just kind of regretting your life choices.<br /> <br /> Anyway, nothing in 3e says beastmen are any less likely to Exalt except by dint of scarcity; if beastmen make up a tiny fraction of the population, they have a vastly reduced likelihood of being Chosen by dint of simply having a massively unlikely factor [&quot;is a beastman&quot;] to line up with all other criteria to be Chosen.<br /> <br /> Of course, if a player wants to play a beastman, the odds of their character being Chosen rise just like if the player wants to play a rich noble or a thaumaturge, to 1:1, because we're playing Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-08T01:50:35-07:00","id":1243733,"title":"","content":"I love the non-mechanical drawbacks. I'm putting together a society of spider-people for the opening plot of my first game. I'd mostly thought of these things as advantages, like not having to deal with pregnancy because they lay eggs. But my starting point was &quot;wouldn't it be cool if some spiderfolk had this sacred rite where they ate their spouse at the funeral.&quot; Anyway, by the time I'd finished, the rite let them pass on knowledge to their spouse, there was massive social pressure to be married to someone older/younger, and the &quot;point&quot; of marriage to this society was so closely tied to the funeral rite that they were more likely to have children with other partners than with their spouse.<br /> <br /> Also, because the rite seemed a bit too powerful to me, I decided that some spirit would be empowering it. She was a functionary in a library before the Contagion/Fair Folk invasion, and a friend in high places got her reassigned as a regional spider-goddess on the fringe of Creation so she wouldn't end up in Yu-Shan's slums. She's obsessed with preserving knowledge now, so she uses her power to help her followers preserve knowledge instead of her assigned duties. The Fair Folk have noticed the lack of oversight and are now slowly imbuing spiders with Wyld energies in preparation for, well, something I'll define in a later plot arc.<br /> <br /> Where did it say beastfolk aren't bred by Lunars any more? I just did a quick ctrl+f through the core pdf and couldn't see that. Obvs canon is canon, but I think I'll probably go with the breeding thing unless the justification is spectacularly exciting and cool. One of my favourite things about Exalted is that it evokes classical mythology over Tolkein, and that feels much more... prominent, I guess, when something lines up with mythology in a way that's taboo in modern western society.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm excited to consider drawbacks and see what else develops. I might end up featuring more beastfolk societies in future stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24421-katamari_naneke","name":"Katamari_Naneke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-08T03:01:05-07:00","id":1243739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katamari_Naneke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237810-balancing-beastmen-adding-flavor-and-depth-through-natural-consequences?p=1243733#post1243733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">not having to deal with pregnancy because they lay eggs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder if any books have ever actually had a reference to a culture with non-mammalian features reproducing in a manner unlike humans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katamari_Naneke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where did it say beastfolk aren't bred by Lunars any more? I just did a quick ctrl+f through the core pdf and couldn't see that. Obvs canon is canon, but I think I'll probably go with the breeding thing unless the justification is spectacularly exciting and cool. One of my favourite things about Exalted is that it evokes classical mythology over Tolkein, and that feels much more... prominent, I guess, when something lines up with mythology in a way that's taboo in modern western society.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's only been said by the developers so far, and it was specifically about Lunars being associated with societies of beastfolk. There's no reason to assume that there aren't individuals who are born from the union of human and animal.<br /> <br /> Besides, there were always supposed to be beastfolk societies that had origins with nothing to do with Lunars, whether they were general mutations or even just a regular person with a regular animal in the Wyld.<br /> <br /> That actually being how it worked with Lunars; it wasn't anything specific to them, they were just advantaged by being able to turn into an animal at will.<br /> <br /> EDIT: The thing that Lunars are doing being said to be using their Charms to create challenges that bestow mutations as blessings upon those who overcome them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 08-08-2018, 06:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-08T03:40:36-07:00","id":1243746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237810-balancing-beastmen-adding-flavor-and-depth-through-natural-consequences?p=1243739#post1243739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if any books have ever actually had a reference to a culture with non-mammalian features reproducing in a manner unlike humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Excepting, of course, the Dragon Kings, who are not human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-08T04:46:24-07:00","id":1243756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237810-balancing-beastmen-adding-flavor-and-depth-through-natural-consequences?p=1243739#post1243739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's only been said by the developers so far, and it was specifically about Lunars being associated with societies of beastfolk. There's no reason to assume that there aren't individuals who are born from the union of human and animal.<br /> <br /> Besides, there were always supposed to be beastfolk societies that had origins with nothing to do with Lunars, whether they were general mutations or even just a regular person with a regular animal in the Wyld.</div> </div> </div> </div>TBH, when they said this, I didn't really see it as a big difference, so much a different emphasis. I always assumed lots of the beastmen in 2nd were just wyld mutants (I mean, that was literally a Wyld mutation you could get randomly in Compass: The Wyld, not to mention minor beastman-esque parts like feathers or fur or animal eyes... all of which are mutations I got at various points on random rolls).<br /> Some, like the snake-men in An-Teng, were specifically mentioned as being descended from a Lunar, but lots of others never had any details of a Lunar ancestor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-08T05:03:07-07:00","id":1243761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Where did it say beastfolk aren't bred by Lunars any more? </div> </div> </div>To be exact, the Devs said that a)many beastfolk aren't related to Lunars, and b)many of those associated with Lunars are created by Lunar rituals, rather than bestiality. It looks like there'll be some charms in the Lunar book that can turn people into beastmen, or something. Obviously, this'll be gone into in the Lunars' book, which isn't out yet.<br /> <br /> I'll have a look in the Ask the Devs thread and see if I can find what they said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-08T14:39:54-07:00","id":1243933,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m now imagining a Liminal made exclusively from the parts of different beast folk.<br /> <br /> A chimeric frankenstein monster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T01:32:42-07:00","id":1244077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237810-balancing-beastmen-adding-flavor-and-depth-through-natural-consequences?p=1243739#post1243739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if any books have ever actually had a reference to a culture with non-mammalian features reproducing in a manner unlike humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd love to see that in future supplements, but if it exists already I'm unaware of it.<br /> <br /> I know that some wyld mutants pick up random animal mutations, and some of them even end up resembling beastfolk as a result. But I'd always understood them as being distinct, even if the distinction isn't always obvious in character.<br /> <br /> I'd be happy with beastfolk being descended from non-Lunars lying with beasts. But I'm gonna be hard to sell on rituals that turn people into beastfolk, or that sort of thing. Still, I am just one fan, and I'm happy to acknowledge this as a matter of taste.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24421-katamari_naneke","name":"Katamari_Naneke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T01:53:54-07:00","id":1244084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katamari_Naneke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237810-balancing-beastmen-adding-flavor-and-depth-through-natural-consequences?p=1244077#post1244077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd love to see that in future supplements, but if it exists already I'm unaware of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the Second Edition approach, I could probably see something like &quot;Egg-layer&quot; being an Abomination that a certain ethnicity happens to inherit, even if my personal inclination would be that it's too dramatic a departure and that beastfolk should be basically human.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how it would fit into Third Edition's approach, and would need to wait and see what the Lunars book actually does with mutations (which will apparently include Supernatural and regular physical Merits). Imbuing the capacity to lay eggs like a bird, reptile, fish or arthropod as a Merit feels a bit odd, and even as a Flaw seems... insufficiently dramatic.<br /> <br /> That said, I have an aforementioned bias, and am framing the subject in those terms.<br /> <br /> I know that some wyld mutants pick up random animal mutations, and some of them even end up resembling beastfolk as a result. But I'd always understood them as being distinct, even if the distinction isn't always obvious in character.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katamari_Naneke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be happy with beastfolk being descended from non-Lunars lying with beasts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I should think that in most instances, that would be expressed as non-Lunars lying with humans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katamari_Naneke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I'm gonna be hard to sell on rituals that turn people into beastfolk, or that sort of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's a question of how one wants to approach Lunars building their distinct armies; sprung from their loins, or converted with witchery and tests of worthiness?<br /> <br /> One thing that I'll say is that associating with the former gave a lot of people this really weird image that Lunars were or ought to be really strongly associated with magic to empower reproduction in various ways.<br /> <br /> If nothing else, transforming existing people rather than having children and waiting several generations for their descendants to sufficiently multiply seems more practical in the short term. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T09:48:42-07:00","id":1244180,"title":"","content":"I agree, in 10 years of playing Exalted, with Lunars as one of the more popular Exalt types (not the most, but quite popular), I've never seen anyone breed a beastmen army. 3 Lunar PCs had kids, producing between them a total of... 2 beastmen (and a bunch of regular humans). Who both disliked their fathers. Most of the beastmen who served the PCs they social-fu'd away from Ma-Ha-Suchi. Much more practical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T10:29:51-07:00","id":1244192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237810-balancing-beastmen-adding-flavor-and-depth-through-natural-consequences?p=1244084#post1244084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the Second Edition approach, I could probably see something like &quot;Egg-layer&quot; being an Abomination that a certain ethnicity happens to inherit, even if my personal inclination would be that it's too dramatic a departure and that beastfolk should be basically human.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how it would fit into Third Edition's approach, and would need to wait and see what the Lunars book actually does with mutations (which will apparently include Supernatural and regular physical Merits). Imbuing the capacity to lay eggs like a bird, reptile, fish or arthropod as a Merit feels a bit odd, and even as a Flaw seems... insufficiently dramatic.<br /> <br /> That said, I have an aforementioned bias, and am framing the subject in those terms.<br /> <br /> I know that some wyld mutants pick up random animal mutations, and some of them even end up resembling beastfolk as a result. But I'd always understood them as being distinct, even if the distinction isn't always obvious in character.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I should think that in most instances, that would be expressed as non-Lunars lying with humans.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think it's a question of how one wants to approach Lunars building their distinct armies; sprung from their loins, or converted with witchery and tests of worthiness?<br /> <br /> One thing that I'll say is that associating with the former gave a lot of people this really weird image that Lunars were or ought to be really strongly associated with magic to empower reproduction in various ways.<br /> <br /> If nothing else, transforming existing people rather than having children and waiting several generations for their descendants to sufficiently multiply seems more practical in the short term.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would contest that beastfolk are distant enough from Lunars in 3e that they can't really be called a distinct component of Lunar armies, because they (edit: specifically, the Lunars) have none of the luxuries that would allow for a signature force. They don't have connections in heaven, they aren't the understudies and apprentices of the Deathlords, and they aren't related to Fair Folk, and they don't gather in the numbers of the Dragon-Blooded. They're scattered, disparate, and more or less isolated from each other; moreover, the fact that there are independent nations of beastfolk that have nothing to do with Lunars produces more distance from the concept. While being able to turn people into beastfolk is a more desirable power than making them the old editions' way, it's something that any sorcerer could do, given the effort of a sufficiently-powerful working. The connection is gone, and one has to ask if it ever should have been there in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 08-09-2018, 02:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T11:36:30-07:00","id":1244225,"title":"","content":"Eh, I'm fine with there being some connection between werewolves and wolfmen, or whatever. Doesn't seem ridiculous. Just not something that should be over-used.<br /> <br /> Also, I can kind of see, since Lunars tend to be further towards the edge of Creation than the Realm, where mutants and beastfolk are more common*, that the Realm's stereotype of Lunar armies is probably &quot;barbarians&quot;, and the Realm's stereotype of what a barbarian is includes frequent mutations, beastmen, etc.<br /> <br /> *Not very common. But more common than in the Realm, so I could well see Realm peasants as imagining the far Threshold is full of cackling Lunar Kings ruling armies of cannibal beastmen who ravage the (still ignorant and savage, but better than the Lunars' servants) regular Threshold humans. Even if this is not really true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T13:27:03-07:00","id":1244258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237810-balancing-beastmen-adding-flavor-and-depth-through-natural-consequences?p=1244225#post1244225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, I'm fine with there being some connection between werewolves and wolfmen, or whatever. Doesn't seem ridiculous. Just not something that should be over-used.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would characterizing them as a signature soldier-type of Lunars not qualify as overuse?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, I can kind of see, since Lunars tend to be further towards the edge of Creation than the Realm, where mutants and beastfolk are more common*, that the Realm's stereotype of Lunar armies is probably &quot;barbarians&quot;, and the Realm's stereotype of what a barbarian is includes frequent mutations, beastmen, etc.<br /> <br /> *Not very common. But more common than in the Realm, so I could well see Realm peasants as imagining the far Threshold is full of cackling Lunar Kings ruling armies of cannibal beastmen who ravage the (still ignorant and savage, but better than the Lunars' servants) regular Threshold humans. Even if this is not really true. </div> </div> </div>Especially if it's not really true. The Dynasts ship in wild animals to make the peasants live in fear of attacks by &quot;vicious beasts&quot;, so it's probably a close fear to have an even more transgressive vision of life off the Isle based on strained, tenuous connections.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T14:33:43-07:00","id":1244275,"title":"","content":"Hmm... Re progenitive Lunars, if you're playing with the kind of time scales for Exalted advancement that Exalted generally holds for NPCs, then Lunars probably mostly can get to thousands strong nations armies of beastmen descendants (at least) simply through 10-15 generations (perhaps 400 years) of no specially huge reproductive rates and no particularly huge reproduction per generation per Lunar, and simply through typical geometric growth and *some* social and economic advantage to being the child of a socially prestigious god-king, with more strengths than weaknesses from your lineage.<br /> <br /> If you're playing in super-fast PC every-crisis-is-happening-RIGHT-NOW advancement time (where you move *up* waaaay faster than the implied averags for NPCs), then yeah, that's not going to do much in terms of having an army / nation of descendants before becoming prominent. So practically as a Lunar you'd probably be working off recruitment, if you were even having Lunar beastmen in your employ. But then I kind of think of that as so much the worse for playing super-fast PC advancement time...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T14:42:45-07:00","id":1244276,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah, you can found a nation and grow it from your family in 400 years. Of course, if you've got 400 years, there's loads of other stuff you can do as well. I think you might well get Lunars who think &quot;my bear-folk descendants are way better than regular humans, I'll have some and have them grow and breed because they're cool and awesome,&quot; or just because, well, lots of people want to see their descendants do well. But I don't think you'd get many who go &quot;bwahaha, I'll breed my own army of elite bear-warriors! In 400 years, I'll be ready to conquer Varang!&quot;<br /> <br /> Whereas with these new rituals to turn soldiers into beastfolk that are apparently going into the Lunar book, beastfolk armies would actually seem much more viable than 2nd ed... which I find interesting, considering the talk of severing the link between beastfolk and Lunars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T15:15:56-07:00","id":1244288,"title":"","content":"Yeah, pretty much agree; having just heard of the idea, personally pretty OK with Lunars whose followers aquire empowering beast characteristics through magical rituals.<br /> <br /> Just also throwing it out there that I'm also fairly OK should it be the case that having armies of loyal beast people who are personal to you (that is not recruited from existing beastpeople tribes and groups) to be something that fairly experienced, &quot;middle aged&quot; Lunars acquire somewhat incidentally to what they're mainly doing - it's somewhat cool in a different flavour to maintain that personal connection and have this be a hallmark of certain types of fairly experienced Lunars who have long led their peoples across the generations and become indivisible from their peoples.<br /> <br /> While I agree as well that it's the ideas that the play experience of young Lunars where they should or can will quickly &quot;build&quot; beastman armies of significant scale to achieve some ends, through lots of reproduction(!), seems like where stuff starts to get weird... (and which was probably an unintended idea when GCG and the early Exalted writers dreamed up ideas of beastmen tribes as the sons and daughters of Lunars?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T17:04:03-07:00","id":1244320,"title":"","content":"I mean, my understanding is that breeding beastfolk was an innovation of a First-Age Lunar, not something that Luna specifically imagined for her chosen at the outset. Perhaps the Lunars developed breeding charms that hurried things along, perhaps they didn't. Given the scale of time that they generally work on, Thousand Streams River and all, I think breeding beastfolk is a viable option. For the short term option, in the modern setting enough beastfolk exist that many aren't tied to any one Lunar, so newly Exalted Lunars can recruit them instead. (Or as well.) Canon Lunars certainly aren't averse to this, there's plenty of beastfolk in Halta who aren't snakefolk or hawkfolk.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I still prefer the idea of them &quot;springing from a Lunar's loins.&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Though your (Isator Levi's) idea in comment #36 about how Merits could be the difference between superficial fingernails and dangerous claws is comparable to Athletic skill might well reconcile the Lunar charms that are probably coming with my view of how beastfolk ought to work. Lunars recruiting beastfolk could use those powers to make sure their animal qualities have hard benefits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24421-katamari_naneke","name":"Katamari_Naneke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T17:30:21-07:00","id":1244324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237810-balancing-beastmen-adding-flavor-and-depth-through-natural-consequences?p=1244275#post1244275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm... Re progenitive Lunars, if you're playing with the kind of time scales for Exalted advancement that Exalted generally holds for NPCs, then Lunars probably mostly can get to thousands strong nations armies of beastmen descendants (at least) simply through 10-15 generations (perhaps 400 years) of no specially huge reproductive rates and no particularly huge reproduction per generation per Lunar, and simply through typical geometric growth and *some* social and economic advantage to being the child of a socially prestigious god-king, with more strengths than weaknesses from your lineage.<br /> <br /> If you're playing in super-fast PC every-crisis-is-happening-RIGHT-NOW advancement time (where you move *up* waaaay faster than the implied averags for NPCs), then yeah, that's not going to do much in terms of having an army / nation of descendants before becoming prominent. So practically as a Lunar you'd probably be working off recruitment, if you were even having Lunar beastmen in your employ. But then I kind of think of that as so much the worse for playing super-fast PC advancement time...</div> </div> </div> </div>But why bother with non-shapeshifting beastfolk when you could probably change someone into a raging Crinos bomb? I mean, if the Garou had Curse of the Wolf to work with in W:tA (or at least, back in the middle ages of the WoD), surely Lunars could have that capacity and then some. Give the angry, crushed masses a fighting chance, or punish mortal Dynasts by making them live out a angsty werewolf story - either way, it feels more distinctly Lunar than something that any of the sorcerers, Fair Folk, or hundreds to thousands of animal gods in Creation could have done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T01:26:15-07:00","id":1244412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237810-balancing-beastmen-adding-flavor-and-depth-through-natural-consequences?p=1244192#post1244192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would contest that beastfolk are distant enough from Lunars in 3e that they can't really be called a distinct component of Lunar armies</div> </div> </div> </div>We have decent examples of beastfolk that have nothing to do with Lunars, but we also have enough examples of Lunars that have something to do with beastfolk, so between that and developer statements, I think that ship has sailed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">they (edit: specifically, the Lunars) have none of the luxuries that would allow for a signature force. They don't have connections in heaven, they aren't the understudies and apprentices of the Deathlords, and they aren't related to Fair Folk, and they don't gather in the numbers of the Dragon-Blooded. They're scattered, disparate, and more or less isolated from each other</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe that the case, in character, for such an association will come in two parts.<br /> <br /> One will Lunars having native powers to bestow mutations upon people, which will apparently tend to involve giving them beast traits. Makes enough sense to me, Lunar magic in general having a bestial quality.<br /> <br /> The other is coming at the question of how and why they build armies from a different direction; they're not the establishment, they're coming in to lead people against the establishment. Lunars don't have an institutionalized process for bestowing them with armies, but they do have a playback of working their way into the heart of marginalized societies and radicalizing them against the Realm. In that space, the capacity to grant them a bunch of physical and supernatural Merits likely serves the need to turn people into fighters (possibly of a tricky kind that the Realm has difficulty handling) fairly quickly. It can also put that Lunar's signature on them, helping to build their terror brand. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">While being able to turn people into beastfolk is a more desirable power than making them the old editions' way, it's something that any sorcerer could do, given the effort of a sufficiently-powerful working.</div> </div> </div> </div>So is shapeshifting.<br /> <br /> More than that, Vance has said outright that Lunars will possess a number of powers that other people would need to be sorcerers to do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The connection is gone</div> </div> </div> </div>It's right there in the Realm's chapter on the Caul, regarding the typical kinds of armies of His Divine Lunar Presence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">one has to ask if it ever should have been there in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the First Edition? Should there have ever been any connection between the fairly straightforward brutal tribal people with animal features, and the fairly straightforward brutal tribal Exalted whose signature trick was turning into a scary person with animal features? I think by the conceits of the time, sure, there should have been a connection.<br /> <br /> The milieu of beastfolk has become more varied and sophisticated, but then, so has that of Lunars; they're not <i>all</i> running the playbook of creating gauntlets to turn petitioners into beastfolk.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T05:46:09-07:00","id":1244456,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t think Lays Eggs should cost any more points than Selective Conception. While it is an enormous physical departure, narratively it isn\u2019t important often enough to be worth more, and even when it comes up, it\u2019s as much a problem as an advantage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T16:07:36-07:00","id":1244651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237810-balancing-beastmen-adding-flavor-and-depth-through-natural-consequences?p=1244412#post1244412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We have decent examples of beastfolk that have nothing to do with Lunars,</div> </div> </div> </div>An entire nation of two different types unified into a single society.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but we also have enough examples of Lunars that have something to do with beastfolk, so between that and developer statements, I think that ship has sailed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I believe that the case, in character, for such an association will come in two parts.<br /> <br /> One will Lunars having native powers to bestow mutations upon people, which will apparently tend to involve giving them beast traits. Makes enough sense to me, Lunar magic in general having a bestial quality.<br /> <br /> The other is coming at the question of how and why they build armies from a different direction; they're not the establishment, they're coming in to lead people against the establishment. Lunars don't have an institutionalized process for bestowing them with armies, but they do have a playback of working their way into the heart of marginalized societies and radicalizing them against the Realm. In that space, the capacity to grant them a bunch of physical and supernatural Merits likely serves the need to turn people into fighters (possibly of a tricky kind that the Realm has difficulty handling) fairly quickly. It can also put that Lunar's signature on them, helping to build their terror brand. </div> </div> </div>Which still leaves them with something less impressive than a WoD power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So is shapeshifting. </div> </div> </div>Presumably something that looks more like in Earthsea, Ladyhawke or with the siblings of the sorcerer from the Conan cartoon than the free-wheeling, unrestricted Lunar variety, at least when it comes to animal-based shapeshifting. No forgetting your true nature or being restricted by time, here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> More than that, Vance has said outright that Lunars will possess a number of powers that other people would need to be sorcerers to do. </div> </div> </div>Technically, that's also been a part of the really weird Sidereal bag, hasn't it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's right there in the Realm's chapter on the Caul, regarding the typical kinds of armies of His Divine Lunar Presence.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> In the First Edition? Should there have ever been any connection between the fairly straightforward brutal tribal people with animal features, and the fairly straightforward brutal tribal Exalted whose signature trick was turning into a scary person with animal features? I think by the conceits of the time, sure, there should have been a connection.<br /> <br /> The milieu of beastfolk has become more varied and sophisticated, but then, so has that of Lunars; they're not <i>all</i> running the playbook of creating gauntlets to turn petitioners into beastfolk. </div> </div> </div>The milieu of beastfolk changed before the first Lunar book was out. CB: Night introduced snakefolk as being fairly well-established in most major urban locales across Creation, and having homes otherwise mostly in southeastern jungles. They're noted for being distrusted for their appearance rather than for any Lunar connections. Moreover, grouping together beings with animal features to the Lunars solely for that reason is a herring so red that in the Realm, only the Scarlet Empress is legally permitted to dine upon it or authorize its capture and culinary preparation. The Lunars number only about 400; that's a drop in the bucket compared to everything else with magical powers and an animal-based appearance. The Lunars shouldn't be any more strongly associated with beastfolk than they are with defending Creation from the Wyld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-11T12:52:12-07:00","id":1244896,"title":"","content":"Before I say anything else, I want to register with you that I feel that you're getting a bit unnecessarily heated about this subject. It's very similar to when you were arguing about the parameters of a Lunar's hybrid body, and it makes me feel as though it's becoming a thing with regards to discussing these Exalted. If it keeps going like this, I wouldn't really want to have such discussions any longer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237810-balancing-beastmen-adding-flavor-and-depth-through-natural-consequences?p=1244651#post1244651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which still leaves them with something less impressive than a WoD power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who is &quot;them&quot; in this sentence: the Lunars bestowing the power, or the beastfolk receiving it?<br /> <br /> Either way, it's an odd comparison, not least because there are many World of Darkness powers running a wide gamut of strengths.<br /> <br /> If we were to compare it to the powers of other actual Exalted, well, I'd say that being able to bestow people with various kinds of Merit is no worse than any currently published Solar Charm to imbue somebody with power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Presumably something that looks more like in Earthsea, Ladyhawke or with the siblings of the sorcerer from the Conan cartoon than the free-wheeling, unrestricted Lunar variety, at least when it comes to animal-based shapeshifting. No forgetting your true nature or being restricted by time, here.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Technically, that's also been a part of the really weird Sidereal bag, hasn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div>What do these points matter? They don't really say anything about the substance of the point that Lunars will have powers that do similar things to what some sorcery can do, and that sorcery being able to do something doesn't invalidate it as a power for Lunars.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The milieu of beastfolk changed before the first Lunar book was out. CB: Night introduced snakefolk as being fairly well-established in most major urban locales across Creation, and having homes otherwise mostly in southeastern jungles. They're noted for being distrusted for their appearance rather than for any Lunar connections.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fine, but it doesn't mean that there was never a basis for connecting Lunars to beastmen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lunars number only about 400; that's a drop in the bucket compared to everything else with magical powers and an animal-based appearance. The Lunars shouldn't be any more strongly associated with beastfolk than they are with defending Creation from the Wyld.</div> </div> </div> </div>In character, there's something to be said for the cultural image that many in the Realm and Threshold might give to beastfolk if it's a not uncommon occurrence for people like that to be attacking them under the banner of a Lunar.<br /> <br /> It's not rational, but then, neither are widespread assaults on Muslim people after an Islamist terrorist group caused a prominent attack, or banning their travel based on the existence of an illicit state founded by such terrorists. It would be perfectly consistent for these folk to be looking at the actions of some beastfolk and coming away with &quot;the Beasts will make off with your children; they'll come after them in the night&quot;.<br /> <br /> Out of character, I would maintain that the connection can be strong, but <b>not universal</b>, based on the common motif between Lunar Exalted and humans with animal features.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-11T20:33:26-07:00","id":1245041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237810-balancing-beastmen-adding-flavor-and-depth-through-natural-consequences?p=1244896#post1244896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Before I say anything else, I want to register with you that I feel that you're getting a bit unnecessarily heated about this subject. It's very similar to when you were arguing about the parameters of a Lunar's hybrid body, and it makes me feel as though it's becoming a thing with regards to discussing these Exalted. If it keeps going like this, I wouldn't really want to have such discussions any longer.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Who is &quot;them&quot; in this sentence: the Lunars bestowing the power, or the beastfolk receiving it?<br /> <br /> Either way, it's an odd comparison, not least because there are many World of Darkness powers running a wide gamut of strengths.</div> </div> </div> </div>And they go in weird places, especially in Werewolf, but we are talking about shapeshifting here. It's not like conjuring up storms or calling the sun back over the horizon at night. Turning someone into a beast is likely vastly more easy for Lunars than for Garou and Fera, and accomplishing a berserker-bomb, probably only slightly more difficult.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If we were to compare it to the powers of other actual Exalted, well, I'd say that being able to bestow people with various kinds of Merit is no worse than any currently published Solar Charm to imbue somebody with power. </div> </div> </div>Making a character a prophet with Presence grants an Essence pool and a concentrated Charm, so it's arguably a closer comparison to having a Lunar-empowered mortal gain an Essence pool and a single animal shape as a Charm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What do these points matter? They don't really say anything about the substance of the point that Lunars will have powers that do similar things to what some sorcery can do, and that sorcery being able to do something doesn't invalidate it as a power for Lunars. </div> </div> </div>For that, you'd really need to get into how Lunar beastfolk might differ from other beastfolk. And if there isn't a difference, that's not really a strong connection.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's fine, but it doesn't mean that there was never a basis for connecting Lunars to beastmen. </div> </div> </div>I'll grant that, but the turnaround seems sharp enough to cause some intense whiplash. Additionally, with the even greater quantity of Lunar-unrelated beastfolk in 3e, it seems like it would make more sense to downplay the Lunar connections than to try to recapture them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In character, there's something to be said for the cultural image that many in the Realm and Threshold might give to beastfolk if it's a not uncommon occurrence for people like that to be attacking them under the banner of a Lunar.<br /> <br /> It's not rational, but then, neither are widespread assaults on Muslim people after an Islamist terrorist group caused a prominent attack, or banning their travel based on the existence of an illicit state founded by such terrorists. It would be perfectly consistent for these folk to be looking at the actions of some beastfolk and coming away with &quot;the Beasts will make off with your children; they'll come after them in the night&quot;.<br /> <br /> Out of character, I would maintain that the connection can be strong, but <b>not universal</b>, based on the common motif between Lunar Exalted and humans with animal features. </div> </div> </div>Few Lunars park themselves in their hybrid forms, though. Also, did you not argue with me, following the release of the Eska writeup for Adversaries, that some hybrid forms might not even look like what people would understand to be like beastfolk? So, even in the case of Eska actually parking herself in her hybrid form, no connection with spiderfolk would be apparent?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T04:28:57-07:00","id":1245083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237810-balancing-beastmen-adding-flavor-and-depth-through-natural-consequences?p=1245041#post1245041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">And they go in weird places, especially in Werewolf, but we are talking about shapeshifting here. It's not like conjuring up storms or calling the sun back over the horizon at night. Turning someone into a beast is likely vastly more easy for Lunars than for Garou and Fera, and accomplishing a berserker-bomb, probably only slightly more difficult.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I seriously do not understand the point that you're trying to make here.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Making a character a prophet with Presence grants an Essence pool and a concentrated Charm, so it's arguably a closer comparison to having a Lunar-empowered mortal gain an Essence pool and a single animal shape as a Charm.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Remind me what the Charm does, and then it can be compared to the various kinds of stat bonuses or expanded capabilities that might be provided by a number of physical and supernatural Merits. I think the approach of &quot;it's called a Charm, so it can only ever be comparable to something else called a Charm&quot; is too simplistic.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">For that, you'd really need to get into how Lunar beastfolk might differ from other beastfolk.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I think that the most important difference in that scenario is the Lunar herself. The values that the Lunar demands in prospective beastfolk, the local cultural and political context of a Lunar going around offering the transformation and people wanting it, and the legacy imprinted in their society by the first generation of beastfolk having come from that association.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Lunars will have Charms of their own to bestow such a thing, so they'll be able to do it on their own terms, rather than the terms of an associated spirit, or traits conferred by initiation into sorcery. It's a thing they will get to do, and can be presumed to do with reasonable frequency. It presumably differs from sorcerers or random powerful spirits by the context in which it is employed; there are probably not <b>zero</b> gods of the right kind who are in opposition to the Realm, but it's probably a less consistent thing.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Sure there's a question of why the Lunars still need to confer blessings in the form of animal traits, to which I say... I don't know. Go ask the developers, why don't you? There's an entire thread for that. Go ask the people that have actually made the decision why the decision has been made, if it matters so much to you.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Few Lunars park themselves in their hybrid forms, though.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I would posit that there are many cases in which a Lunar only needs to assume Deadly Beastman Transformation once in front of a sufficiently large number of people, and they and everybody they tell about it will remember that form forever.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">did you not argue with me, following the release of the Eska writeup for Adversaries, that some hybrid forms might not even look like what people would understand to be like beastfolk? So, even in the case of Eska actually parking herself in her hybrid form, no connection with spiderfolk would be apparent?</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The simplest answer to this is that I don't think it works to reduce things down to one Lunar, and that it's reasonable to assume that most people in Creation who think a lot about Lunars imagine them more in terms of people who look like Strength of Many or Ma-Ha-Suchi.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T22:44:48-07:00","id":1245337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237810-balancing-beastmen-adding-flavor-and-depth-through-natural-consequences?p=1237968#post1237968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well Lunar-created beastmen are different in 3E. They're not the offspring of Lunars. Instead, they are humans who passed a Lunar's trial/initiation and were blessed with beastmen mutations.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wait a minute--where was this from?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T22:44:48-07:00","id":1245338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237810-balancing-beastmen-adding-flavor-and-depth-through-natural-consequences?p=1237968#post1237968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well Lunar-created beastmen are different in 3E. They're not the offspring of Lunars. Instead, they are humans who passed a Lunar's trial/initiation and were blessed with beastmen mutations.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wait a minute--where was this from?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T22:46:40-07:00","id":1245339,"title":"","content":"Vance said Lunars will have a charm for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T05:54:14-07:00","id":1245425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NewK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237810-balancing-beastmen-adding-flavor-and-depth-through-natural-consequences?p=1245337#post1245337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Wait a minute--where was this from?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been discussed a few times in the &quot;Ask the Dev&quot; thread. The ability to create Beastmen is now a charm effect. Though we don't know any of the specifics at this time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T06:00:13-07:00","id":1245427,"title":"","content":"Several charm effects, in fact.<br /> <br /> Indications are they have one charm to just slap mutations on someone, and further up the tree they can bless an area so it becomes a trial that will bestow mutations on anyone who passes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}